      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "HISTORY AND ADMISSION FINDINGS",
          "content": "A 19-year-old man was admitted to our hospital because of fever and exhaustion. During his hospital stay he had pain in the back and flanks."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INVESTIGATIONS",
          "content": "The electrocardiogram (ECG) revealed ST-segment elevation in V1-V3, similar to that occurring in myocardial infarction. Renal function was decreased with proteinuria and the platelet count was decreased The symptoms and clinical findings aroused the suspicion of a Hantavirus infection, which was confirmed by antibody tests."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "TREATMENT AND COURSE",
          "content": "The patient was treated symptomatically with paracetamol. After 5 days the patient felt better and had a normal temperature. The thrombocyte count and renal function normalised after 10 days in hospital."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "In case of a suspected peril-/ myocarditis a Hantavirus infection should be considered as a possible cause, which should be clarified by antibody tests."
        }
      ]},
